{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"21":{"eng-name":"Funerals (Kitab Al-Jana'iz)","ara-name":"كتاب الجنائز"}},"section_detail":{"21":{"hadithnumber_first":3089,"hadithnumber_last":3241,"arabicnumber_first":3089,"arabicnumber_last":3241}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":3092,"arabicnumber":3092,"text":"Rapporté par Umm al-Ala : Le Messager d’Allah ﷺ m’a rendu visite alors que j’étais malade. Il a dit : « Réjouis-toi, Umm al-Ala, car Allah efface les péchés d’un musulman par la maladie, comme le feu enlève les impuretés de l’or et de l’argent. »","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Hasan"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Hasan"}],"reference":{"book":21,"hadith":4},"chapter":{"id":3,"ara-name":"باب عِيَادَةِ النِّسَاءِ","eng-name":"Visiting Sick Women","isFirstHadith":true}}]}